NAME
       mkfs - create a file system (front end)

SYNOPSIS
       mkfs [-t TYPE] [TYPE-OPTIONS] DEVICE

DESCRIPTION
       mkfs is a small front end: "mkfs -t TYPE" runs the program mkfs.TYPE
       (mkfs.xfs, mkfs.ext4, mkfs.vfat...) with the remaining arguments.
       Without -t it makes ext2. It is usually clearer to run mkfs.TYPE
       directly.

OPTIONS
       -t, --type TYPE
              The file system type: xfs, ext4, ext3, ext2, vfat.

       -V     Show the command mkfs runs.

EXAMPLES
           mkfs -t xfs /dev/vdb1
           mkfs -t ext4 -L logs /dev/vgdata/logs

SEE ALSO
       mkfs.xfs(8), mke2fs(8), mkfs.fat(8), mkswap(8)
